Round 1 defects and this round's fixes:
1. Role-gate defect (no [~] task in the phase): the `Task (Green 4d)` row is now `[~]`, and its pass cases name the round 2 cases.
2. Forge contract defect: R-P4-11 and R-P4-12 now build the job through one fixture helper. The job, the candidate, and `lineArt` hold 'ready'. The helper holds the contract fields of advantage-forge book-pictures.ts at 11a06b9c (jobId, reviews, failures, renderEvidenceFile, errors, formatVersion, technique, and the StorytimeJob fields). No 'selected' status remains; the contract allows only 'ready', 'pending', and 'failed'. New R-P4-15: the adapter must throw for a job with status 'pending', for a job with status 'failed', and for a ready job with selectedVersion null; a ready-job anchor blocks an always-throwing adapter. New R-P4-16: the batch driver must report such a row as fail with a reason string.
3. Source-text-search defect: R-P4-13 is now a behaviour test. Run 1 spawns make-readers-pdf.ts with --level 2 --weeks 1 --final --workbook, HOME set to a new temp folder, and WORKBOOKS_ROOT set to a temp repo copy. The copy holds the shipped w01.json and 17 of the 18 requested picture files. The placeholder files are 1 x 1 PNGs, because the CLI preflight is an existence check; the stage-one measurement is the batch driver's job, not the CLI's. The run must exit nonzero, name the missing picture, and leave no output file and no readers-* output folder under <home>/Desktop/print-ready. Run 2 (the same version) must stop on the same missing picture, not on an "output exists" error. At the role base the case fails, because run 1 creates the readers-l2-w1-v1 folder before the missing-picture stop. The preflight stops before Chrome, so the test needs no browser; one attempt takes about 1 s.
4. New fact (PM, 2026-11-01: the Forge line art is 1-bit after the enlargement): new R-P4-17. Fixtures: 4000 x 3000 line art as a two-colour palette PNG (sharp .toColourspace('b-w').png({ palette: true, colors: 2 }); IHDR colour type 3, bit depth 1), and as a hand-made grayscale PNG (colour type 0, bit depth 1, written in the test with node:zlib). The test proves the IHDR bit depth of both written files. Both files must pass checkStorytimePicture. Result at the role base: PASS. Classification: guard case, not a Red case. Reason: sharp expands a 1-bit file to 8-bit uchar raw data with 3 channels, so the current measure loop reads it correctly. The guard keeps that acceptance under future changes to picture-check.ts. A probe of the sharp .png({ bitdepth: 1 }) option showed that sharp 0.34.5 ignores it and writes an 8-bit file, so the test uses the palette route and the hand-made route.

